    #   Where:
    #     0.01 = Amplitude (maximum 1% correction)
    #     0.001 = Angular frequency (day⁻¹)
    #     t = Time in days
    #
    # VALUE RANGE:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   δ_def ∈ [-0.01, +0.01]
    #   Correction factor (1 + δ_def) ∈ [0.99, 1.01]
    #   Maximum perturbation: ±1% of Ug1
    #
    # OSCILLATION PERIOD:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   ω = 0.001 day⁻¹ (angular frequency)
    #   T = 2π/ω = 2π/0.001 ≈ 6283.2 days ≈ 17.22 years
    #   
    #   This ~17.22 year period does NOT correspond to:
    #     • 11-year solar cycle (Schwabe cycle)
    #     • 22-year Hale cycle (magnetic polarity reversal)
    #   May represent:
