    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # ρ_vac,[SCm] - SUPERCONDUCTIVE MATERIAL VACUUM ENERGY DENSITY
    # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    #
    # DEFINITION:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   ρ_vac,[SCm] = 7.09 × 10⁻³⁷ J/m³ (for Sun, level 13)
    #
    #   This is the vacuum energy density associated with Superconductive
    #   Material [SCm], a massless, extra-universal material present in all
    #   matter that reacts with Universal Aether [UA] to build physical
    #   elements and drive universal dynamics.
    #
    # VALUE:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   ρ_vac,[SCm] = 7.09 × 10⁻³⁷ J/m³ (Sun, quantum level 13)
    #
    #   Units: J/m³ = kg·m⁻¹·s⁻² (energy per unit volume)
    #
    # SCALING ACROSS QUANTUM LEVELS:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   Unlike ρ_vac,A (constant), [SCm] vacuum density SCALES with level:
    #
    #     Level 10 (atomic): ρ_vac,[SCm] = 1.60 × 10¹⁹ J/m³
    #     Level 13 (solar):  ρ_vac,[SCm] = 7.09 × 10⁻³⁷ J/m³
    #
    #   Scale ratio: 10¹⁹ / 10⁻³⁷ = 10⁵⁶ (56 orders of magnitude!)
    #
    #   This reflects [SCm]'s influence being MORE pronounced at smaller
    #   scales (atomic interactions, proton stability) and diminishing at
    #   larger scales (stellar dynamics).
    #
    # COMPARISON WITH OTHER VACUUM DENSITIES (Solar Scale):
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   • ρ_vac,[SCm] = 7.09 × 10⁻³⁷ J/m³  ← SMALLEST at solar scale
    #   • ρ_vac,Ui    = 2.84 × 10⁻³⁶ J/m³  (4× [SCm])
    #   • ρ_vac,[UA]  = 7.09 × 10⁻³⁶ J/m³  (10× [SCm])
    #   • ρ_vac,A     = 1.00 × 10⁻²³ J/m³  (10¹⁴× [SCm], CONSTANT)
    #
    #   Comparison with physical densities:
    #   • CMB:         ~4 × 10⁻¹⁴ J/m³ (much larger than ρ_vac,[SCm])
    #   • ISM:         ~10⁻¹³ to 10⁻¹¹ J/m³
    #   • Dark Energy: ~7 × 10⁻¹⁰ J/m³ (cosmological constant)
    #   • QFT Vacuum:  ~10¹¹³ J/m³ (theoretical, renormalized)
    #
    # RELATIONSHIP TO [UA]:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   At solar scale (level 13):
    #     ρ_vac,[UA] / ρ_vac,[SCm] = 7.09×10⁻³⁶ / 7.09×10⁻³⁷ = 10
    #
    #   [UA] is exactly 10× larger than [SCm] at every scale, reflecting
    #   the 10:1 hierarchy between Universal Aether and Superconductive
    #   Material vacuum energy densities.
    #
    # ROLE IN UNIFIED FIELD EQUATION:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   ρ_vac,[SCm] appears in multiple terms of F_U:
    #
    #   1. Ug1 (Internal Dipole):
    #      μ_s(t, ρ_vac,[SCm]) - magnetic moment depends on [SCm]
    #
    #   2. Ug2 (Outer Field Bubble):
    #      (ρ_vac,[UA] + ρ_vac,[SCm]) × M_s / r² - combined vacuum scaling
    #
    #   3. Ug3 (Magnetic Strings Disk):
    #      B_j(r, θ, t, ρ_vac,[SCm]) - magnetic field strength
    #
    #   4. Ug4 (Star-BH Interactions):
    #      ρ_vac,[SCm] × M_BH / d_g - gravitational interaction scaling
    #
    #   5. U_i (Universal Inertia):
    #      ρ_vac,[SCm] × ρ_vac,[UA] × ω_s × ... - inertial resistance
    #
    #   6. A_μν (Universal Cosmic Aether):
    #      T_s^μν(ρ_vac,[UA], ρ_vac,[SCm], ...) - stress-energy tensor
    #
    # PHENOMENA AFFECTED:
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   • Nebular Dynamics (Drawing 32): Magnetic strings' fields, dust trails
    #   • Star Formation (Drawing 33): Gravitational collapse, angular momentum
    #   • Quasar Jets (Drawing 1): Near-lossless energy transfer
    #   • Final Parsec Problem (Drawing 3): SMBH binary energy extraction
    #   • Galactic Disk Stability: Magnetic field contributions
    #
    # EXAMPLE CALCULATION (Sun at t=0):
    # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    #   In Ug2:
    #     ρ_vac,[UA] + ρ_vac,[SCm] = 7.09×10⁻³⁶ + 7.09×10⁻³⁷ = 7.80×10⁻³⁶ J/m³
    #
    #   The combined [UA]+[SCm] vacuum density is dominated by [UA] (~91%),
    #   with [SCm] providing ~9% contribution. This ratio reflects [SCm]'s
